# The Lockheed Martin F-22A Raptor's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/f22.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# There is no flap lever on this aeroplane: the flight computer schedules the
# trailing-edge flaps on speed, full down below 180 knots and in above 255,
# so the flap items below read what it has done rather than what the pilot
# has asked for. The speedbrake is out or in and nothing between, and it is
# flown with the flaps, ailerons and rudders rather than a board of its own.
# Its two F119s light their reheat above a throttle of 0.99, which is what
# "into reheat" and "no reheat" mean here, and the aeroplane holds Mach 1.7
# without ever lighting it.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done and the aeroplane clear to start
confirm Strapped in, harness tight and the ejection seat pins stowed
confirm Oxygen on, mask checked and the canopy clear
confirm Weapons bay doors shut and the master arm off
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Both throttles closed
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 35.0 Port engine running
check propulsion/engine[1]/n1 >= 35.0 Starboard engine running
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
confirm Brakes and nose wheel steering checked as the aeroplane first moves
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.40 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 25.0 30.5 Trailing-edge flaps down, as the flight computer sets them below 180 knots
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Pitch trim set for the take-off
confirm Controls free and correct, and the canopy closed and locked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.99 Both throttles fully forward, into reheat
check velocities/vc-kts >= 130.0 Ease the nose up at 130 knots

phase climb
check gear/gear-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage lever up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage locked up
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Trailing-edge flaps in, as they come once past 255 knots
range velocities/vc-kts 300.0 420.0 Climb at 300 to 420 knots
confirm Engine instruments checked, and the fuel watched while the reheat is lit

phase cruise
range velocities/mach 1.40 1.80 Supercruise between Mach 1.4 and 1.8
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.99 Military power, and no reheat to hold it
range position/h-sl-ft 30000.0 50000.0 Level between 30,000 and 50,000 feet
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Trailing-edge flaps in
confirm Fuel checked against the leg still to fly

phase descent
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm >= 0.99 Speedbrake out, which on this aeroplane is all of it or none
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.0 0.60 Throttles back for the descent
check velocities/vc-kts <= 450.0 Down at no more than 450 knots
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure

phase approach
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in for the approach
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 25.0 30.5 Trailing-edge flaps back down of their own accord
range velocities/vc-kts 150.0 180.0 Approach at 150 to 180 knots

phase landing
range velocities/vc-kts 140.0 165.0 Over the threshold at 140 to 165 knots
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttles closed in the flare
confirm Hold the nose high after touchdown, then lower it and brake straight

phase after-landing
check position/h-agl-ft <= 50.0 Down and rolling
check velocities/vc-kts <= 40.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to a taxi power
confirm Master arm off, weapons bay doors shut and the landing light out
